<title>SWEDEN: Sweden's Skandia gets Japan approval.</title>
<headline>Sweden's Skandia gets Japan approval.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish insurer Skandia said on Wednesday it had gained approval from Japan's finance ministry to start selling insurance in Japan.  </p>
<p>Skandia said it had received approval for savings and life assurance sales in Japan.</p>
<p>&quot;This means that we now have access to the largest life insurance market in the world,&quot; said Skandia's Malcolm Campbell.</p>
<p>-- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
